spans.s:
अरुण॑ f. आ (ved. also ई) ruddy, light-brown, yellowish.
m. redness, pers. as Aruṇa, the Dawn, conceived as the charioteer of
the Sun;
 the Sun itself;
 N. of an old teacher etc. f. ई a red cow;
 the
dawn. n. redness, gold, ruby.

आरुण m. ई f. descendant of Aruṇa;
 f. आ॑रुणी also a
red mare.

अरुन्धती॑ f. cert. plant;
 N. of the wife of Vasiṣṭha,
conceived as a star in the Great Bear.

अरुषं॑ f. अ॑रुषी red, fire-coloured. m. the Sun, day. f.
the Dawn;
 a red mare, pl. flames, conceived as the team of Agni.

आ॑रुणि m. ई f. descendant of Aruṇa;
 f. आ॑रुणी also a
red mare.

आरूढ a. mounted, ridden by (—˚), got, obtained;
 act.
(having) mounted, riding, sitting or standing on (loc., acc. or —˚);
come forth, risen;
 fallen into, got to (acc. or —˚).
